   213	\paragraph{Repeating the comparison on six new markets (Q4).} The registered B3--R3 gain-and-efficiency comparison under D2+H3 passes on \site{r_q4_k} of the six markets (Table~\ref{tab:q4}), and all three passes (fresh1, fresh3, fresh4) are about the prescribed search procedure. On every market the estimated B3 minus R3 gain difference is positive and R3 keeps its efficiency condition; where the comparison fails, the difference is smaller than the registered threshold, not reversed: \site{r_q4_f0} on fresh0, \site{r_q4_f2} on fresh2, and \site{r_q4_f5} on fresh5, against \site{r_q4_f1} on fresh1. R3's efficiency on fresh2, the lowest, is \site{r_q4_f2_eff}. The decisions on fresh0, fresh1, fresh3, and fresh4 are about the prescribed search procedure (fresh0 and fresh3 through their references; addendum). The registered prediction of at least five passing markets failed. Q4 does not test the complete amended claim of the first test. Table~\ref{tab:ph-q4} (exploratory) splits each market's difference: on every market it is almost all attacked profit, R3's audit spending sits at its allowance, and its served share is near one, so the failing markets differ from the passing ones in the size of the attacked-profit reduction rather than in a different mechanism.
